          <span class="pill-badge">Systemic Analysis</span>
          <h2 class="section-title">Why Do Teachers Lack Real-Time Mental Health Support at Work?</h2>
          <p class="section-subtitle">
            While corporate environments have increasingly adopted on-demand wellness benefits and mental health days, schools remain structured around rigid bell schedules where an educator cannot step away even for a moment of acute distress.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="problem-grid">
          <!-- Card 1 -->
          <div class="problem-card">
            <div class="problem-icon-box red">
              <svg width="26" height="26" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"></path><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"></polyline><line x1="16" y1="13" x2="8" y2="13"></line><line x1="16" y1="17" x2="8" y2="17"></line><polyline points="10 9 9 9 8 9"></polyline></svg>
            </div>
            <h3>Excessive Administrative & Instructional Overload</h3>
            <p>
              Teachers balance instructional delivery with endless standardized documentation, individualized education plans (IEPs), parent communications, hall duty, and lesson planning—often spanning 55+ hours weekly without buffer time.
            </p>
            <span class="problem-evidence-tag">Over 60% work uncompensated overtime</span>
          </div>

          <!-- Card 2 -->
          <div class="problem-card">
            <div class="problem-icon-box amber">
              <svg width="26" height="26" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M17 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H5a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"></path><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"></circle><path d="M23 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"></path><path d="M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"></path></svg>
            </div>
            <h3>School Counselors Assigned Exclusively to Students</h3>
            <p>
              While schools employ guidance counselors and social workers, their caseloads are legally and practically reserved for students. In over 88% of public schools, there is zero designated mental health personnel for adult staff.
            </p>
            <span class="problem-evidence-tag">Average student-to-counselor ratio: 408:1</span>
          </div>

          <!-- Card 3 -->
          <div class="problem-card">
            <div class="problem-icon-box purple">
              <svg width="26" height="26" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="M8 15s1.5 2 4 2 4-2 4-2"></path><line x1="9" y1="9" x2="9.01" y2="9"></line><line x1="15" y1="9" x2="15.01" y2="9"></line></svg>
            </div>
            <h3>The "Martyrdom Culture" & Stigma Around Vulnerability</h3>
            <p>
              Educators are socially pressured to be endlessly resilient, selfless figures. Admitting mental exhaustion or panic is frequently stigmatized as incompetence, weakness, or letting down one's students and colleagues.
            </p>
            <span class="problem-evidence-tag">61% worry disclosure damages careers</span>
          </div>

          <!-- Card 4 -->
          <div class="problem-card">
            <div class="problem-icon-box blue">
              <svg width="26" height="26" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"></polyline></svg>
            </div>
            <h3>No Coverage for Basic Breaks or Quiet Respite</h3>
            <p>
              Due to severe substitute shortages, teachers cannot step outside the room even for 5 minutes of regulated breathing. Planning periods are routinely confiscated for emergency classroom coverage or mandatory meetings.
            </p>
            <span class="problem-evidence-tag">Vanishing personal bio & lunch breaks</span>
          </div>

          <!-- Card 5 -->
          <div class="problem-card">
            <div class="problem-icon-box teal">
              <svg width="26" height="26" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><rect x="2" y="3" width="20" height="14" rx="2" ry="2"></rect><line x1="8" y1="21" x2="16" y2="21"></line><line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12" y2="21"></line></svg>
            </div>
            <h3>Outdated & Inflexible EAP Architecture</h3>
            <p>
              District Employee Assistance Programs (EAPs) rely on 1-800 hotlines requiring intake calls during business hours, followed by multi-week waitlists for off-campus clinics. They fail completely at acute, 10-minute workday crises.
            </p>
            <span class="problem-evidence-tag">Average intake wait time: 14 to 28 days</span>
          </div>

          <!-- Card 6 -->
          <div class="problem-card">
            <div class="problem-icon-box slate">
              <svg width="26" height="26" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M3 9l9-7 9 7v11a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2z"></path><polyline points="9 22 9 12 15 12 15 22"></polyline></svg>
            </div>
            <h3>Absence of Dedicated Staff Sanctuary Spaces</h3>
            <p>
              Faculty lounges are often noisy, crowded with copy machines and staff meetings, offering zero sensory relief or psychological privacy where an educator can reset after de-escalating a classroom crisis.
            </p>
            <span class="problem-evidence-tag">Zero sensory quiet rooms in 92% of schools</span>
          </div>
        </div>

